+*   **Variance:** The method exhibits noticeable variance across different runs due to the stochastic nature of subsampling and farthest point sampling [S1, unofficial]. Reported values are averaged over multiple runs to provide a more reliable evaluation [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The training time is reduced by a factor proportional to the sparsity of the active set. The active set update step has sublinear complexity $O(M \cdot N)$ where $M$ is the number of subsampled views and $N$ is the number of Gaussians, compared to $O(V \cdot N)$ for full updates where $V$ is the total number of views [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Memory usage is similar to standard OIT-based 3DGS, requiring storage for pre-rendered images for each training view. However, it avoids the memory overhead of storing depth-sorted lists per pixel [S1, unofficial].
